0340-negroni-wlan-ios-iface: Wi-Fi, iOS side part 1: the IODeviceTree "wlan" entry (wifid's launchd job needs it:
_LimitLoadToDeviceTree "wlan"; without it wifid never runs and Settings greys out Wi-Fi), en0 (BSD interface KPI,
Ethernet, subfamily Wi-Fi, MAC of WMI READY), the property-only IO80211Controller + IONetworkInterface services
(IO80211InterfaceRole "Infrastructure", IOInterfaceName en0, no user client -> IO80211.framework ioctl path), the
worker thread between the driver seam (0326 negroni_wlan_api.h) and Apple80211 (0341), link state +
KEV_DL_LINK_ON/OFF (en0 up exactly while CONNECTED; FAILED/OFF take it down), joins with a sequence number
and a 40 s time-out, RX in one 2 KiB cluster mbuf (ue0 pattern), a soft radio switch, and a fake radio (negroniwlan_ios=2) for UI tests without the chip.
Needs 0341 (negroni_apple80211.c) to link. Derived from HakiOS hakios.wlan.cpp / hakios.net.c / hakios.sta.c
(APSL 2.0, notices kept). Details: patches/xnu/README-wifi.md "0340-0341".

